158:
159: ## 4. Data Model Overview
160:
161: While full schema design belongs in Phase 0 (Section 10), the following conceptual entities must exist and must be understood by every engine:
162:
163: - **Lead** — identity, contact info, source, category, current status, assigned admin/counselor.
164: - **Workflow** — current state, state history (audit trail of transitions), active scheduled jobs tied to this lead, cancellation flags.
165: - **Conversation** — every inbound and outbound message, tagged with channel (WhatsApp, Instagram, etc.), direction, timestamp, and template/content reference used.
166: - **Tasks** — pending human actions generated by the system (e.g., "Call Rahul," "Review payment," "Approve scholarship").
167: - **Calendar** — all scheduled calls/meetings/demos linked to the lead, admin availability, reminders.
168: - **Timeline** — the immutable chronological event log for the lead (see Engine 5, Section 8.5) — this is what every automation reads before acting.
169: - **Analytics** — real-time rollups both per-lead and system-wide (see Engine 9, Section 8.9).
170:
171: **Key principle:** every future automation decision reads from the Timeline before acting. No engine acts blindly — it always checks "what has already happened to this lead" first (see Follow-up Engine "Evaluate Situation" pattern, Section 8.6).
